<DemoExample Title="Dynamic ComboBox" RazorCode="@example15RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example15CsharpCode" Id="example15">
    <div>When the <b>Dynamic</b> parameter is true, a text typed into the ComboBox that matches no existing item can be added as a new item; <b>DynamicValueGenerator</b> generates the value of the new item and <b>OnDynamicAdd</b> notifies about the addition.</div>
    <div class="example-content">
        <br />
        <BitDropdown @bind-Value="comboBoxValueSample3"
                     Combo Dynamic Responsive
                     Items="comboBoxCustoms"
                     Placeholder="Select an option"
                     NameSelectors="comboBoxNameSelectors"
                     Label="Single select combo box & dynamic"
                     OnDynamicAdd="(Product item) => HandleOnDynamicAdd(item)"
                     DynamicValueGenerator="@((Product item) => item.Text ?? "")" />
        <br />
        <div>Value: @comboBoxValueSample3</div>
    </div>
    <br /><br /><br /><br />
    <div>Combining the <b>Combo</b>, <b>Chips</b> and <b>Dynamic</b> parameters, new items get added by pressing the enter key (or the add button of the responsive panel on mobile) and render as removable chips.</div>
    <br />
    <div class="example-content">
        <br />
        <BitDropdown @bind-Value="comboBoxValueSample4"
                     Responsive
                     Combo Chips Dynamic
                     Items="comboBoxCustoms"
                     Placeholder="Select an option"
                     NameSelectors="comboBoxNameSelectors"
                     Label="Single select combo box, chips & dynamic"
                     OnDynamicAdd="(Product item) => HandleOnDynamicAdd(item)"
                     DynamicValueGenerator="@((Product item) => item.Text ?? "")" />
        <br />
        <div>Value: @comboBoxValueSample4</div>
        <br /><br />
        <BitDropdown @bind-Values="comboBoxValues3"
                     Responsive
                     MultiSelect
                     Combo Chips Dynamic
                     Items="comboBoxCustoms"
                     Placeholder="Select options"
                     NameSelectors="comboBoxNameSelectors"
                     Label="Multi select combo box, chips & dynamic"
                     OnDynamicAdd="(Product item) => HandleOnDynamicAdd(item)"
                     DynamicValueGenerator="@((Product item) => item.Text ?? "")" />
        <br />
        <div>Values: @string.Join(',', comboBoxValues3)</div>
    </div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Keyboard navigation" RazorCode="@example16RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example16CsharpCode" Id="example16" PreventRenderForMcpClient>
    <div>
        The dropdown is fully operable with the keyboard: <b>Enter</b>, <b>Space</b> and the arrow keys open the callout,
        <b>ArrowUp</b> and <b>ArrowDown</b> move the focus between the items, <b>Home</b> and <b>End</b> jump to the first and last item,
        <b>PageUp</b> and <b>PageDown</b> jump several items at a time, typing characters moves the focus to the next matching item,
        <b>Enter</b> and <b>Space</b> select the focused item and <b>Escape</b> closes the callout.
        In virtualize mode only the rendered items take part in the type-ahead, since the ones that have not been
        rendered yet have no text to match against.
    </div>
    <br />
    <div class="example-content">
        <BitDropdown Label="Single select"
                     Items="GetBasicCustoms()"
                     NameSelectors="nameSelectors"
                     Placeholder="Select an item" />
        <br /><br />
        <BitDropdown Label="Multi select"
                     MultiSelect
                     Items="GetBasicCustoms()"
                     Placeholder="Select items"
                     NameSelectors="nameSelectors" />
    </div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Select all" RazorCode="@example17RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example17CsharpCode" Id="example17" PreventRenderForMcpClient>
    <div>
        When the <b>ShowSelectAll</b> parameter is true, a select all item renders at the top of the callout of the
        multi select dropdown that selects or clears all items at once and shows an indeterminate state when only
        some items are selected. Disabled items are skipped, the <b>SelectAllText</b> parameter customizes its text
        and combined with the search box, it only applies to the search result. It is not available when the
        items come from an <b>ItemsProvider</b>, since the items that are not loaded yet cannot be selected.
    </div>
    <br />
    <div class="example-content">
        <BitDropdown @bind-Values="selectAllValues"
                     MultiSelect
                     ShowSelectAll
                     Items="GetBasicCustoms()"
                     NameSelectors="nameSelectors"
                     Placeholder="Select items"
                     Label="Select all" />
        <br />
        <div>Values: @string.Join(',', selectAllValues)</div>
        <br /><br />
        <BitDropdown MultiSelect
                     ShowSelectAll
                     ShowSearchBox
                     SelectAllText="Select all of them"
                     Items="GetBasicCustoms()"
                     NameSelectors="nameSelectors"
                     Placeholder="Select items"
                     DefaultValue="@string.Empty"
                     SearchBoxPlaceholder="Search items"
                     Label="Custom text & search" />
    </div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Selection limit" RazorCode="@example18RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example18CsharpCode" Id="example18" PreventRenderForMcpClient>
    <div>
        The <b>MaxSelectedItems</b> parameter limits the number of items that can be selected in the multi select
        dropdown; once the limit is reached, the remaining items become disabled until an item gets unselected.
    </div>
    <br />
    <div class="example-content">
        <BitDropdown @bind-Values="maxSelectedValues"
                     MultiSelect
                     MaxSelectedItems="2"
                     Items="GetBasicCustoms()"
                     NameSelectors="nameSelectors"
                     Placeholder="Select up to 2 items"
                     Label="Max 2 items" />
        <br />
        <div>Values: @string.Join(',', maxSelectedValues)</div>
    </div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Empty state" RazorCode="@example19RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example19CsharpCode" Id="example19" PreventRenderForMcpClient>
    <div>
        When there is no item to show in the callout (an empty list or a search without a result), the dropdown
        renders a message that can be customized using the <b>EmptyText</b> and <b>EmptyTemplate</b> parameters.
    </div>
    <br />
    <div class="example-content">
        <BitDropdown Label="Default"
                     Items="emptyCustoms"
                     NameSelectors="nameSelectors"
                     Placeholder="Select an item"
                     TItem="Product" TValue="string" />
        <br /><br />
        <BitDropdown Label="EmptyText"
                     Items="emptyCustoms"
                     NameSelectors="nameSelectors"
                     Placeholder="Select an item"
                     EmptyText="There is nothing here!"
                     TItem="Product" TValue="string" />
        <br /><br />
        <BitDropdown Label="EmptyTemplate"
                     Items="emptyCustoms"
                     NameSelectors="nameSelectors"
                     Placeholder="Select an item"
                     TItem="Product" TValue="string">
            <EmptyTemplate>
                <div class="custom-drp custom-drp-empty">
                    <BitIcon IconName="@BitIconName.SearchIssue" />
                    <div>Nothing to show!</div>
                </div>
            </EmptyTemplate>
        </BitDropdown>
        <br /><br />
        <BitDropdown Label="Search without result"
                     ShowSearchBox
                     Items="GetBasicCustoms()"
                     NameSelectors="nameSelectors"
                     Placeholder="Select an item"
                     SearchBoxPlaceholder="Search for anything" />
    </div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Virtualization" RazorCode="@example20RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example20CsharpCode" Id="example20">
    <div>The <b>Virtualize</b> parameter renders only the visible items instead of the whole list, keeping the dropdown fast with thousands of items — either over a local <b>Items</b> collection or by loading pages on demand through an <b>ItemsProvider</b> (with <b>InitialSelectedItems</b> pre-selecting values that have not been loaded yet). The <b>VirtualizePlaceholder</b> template renders in place of the items that are still loading.</div>
    <br /><br /><br />
    <div class="example-content">
        <div>With <b>Items</b>:</div><br />
        <BitDropdown Label="Single select"
                     Virtualize
                     Items="virtualizeCustoms1"
                     Placeholder="Select an item"
                     NameSelectors="nameSelectors" />
        <br />
        <BitDropdown Label="Multi select"
                     Virtualize
                     MultiSelect
                     Items="virtualizeCustoms2"
                     Placeholder="Select items"
                     NameSelectors="nameSelectors" />
        <br /><br /><br /><br />
        <div>With <b>ItemsProvider</b>:</div><br />
        <BitDropdown Label="Single select"
                     Virtualize
                     ItemsProvider="LoadItems"
                     Placeholder="Select an item"
                     NameSelectors="nameSelectors" />
        <br />
        <BitDropdown Label="Multi select"
                     Virtualize
                     MultiSelect
                     ItemsProvider="LoadItems"
                     Placeholder="Select items"
                     NameSelectors="nameSelectors" />
        <br />
        <BitDropdown Label="VirtualizePlaceholder"
                     Virtualize
                     ItemsProvider="LoadItems"
                     Placeholder="Select an item"
                     NameSelectors="nameSelectors"
                     TItem="Product" TValue="string">
            <VirtualizePlaceholder>
                <div style="padding:0 0.5rem;color:gray">Loading @(context.Index)...</div>
            </VirtualizePlaceholder>
        </BitDropdown>
        <br /><br /><br /><br />
        <div>With <b>ItemsProvider and InitialSelectedItems</b>:</div><br />
        <BitDropdown Label="Single select"
                     Virtualize
                     ItemsProvider="LoadItems"
                     Placeholder="Select an item"
                     InitialSelectedItems="initialSelectedItem"
                     NameSelectors="nameSelectors" />
        <br />
        <BitDropdown Label="Multi select"
                     Virtualize
                     MultiSelect
                     ItemsProvider="LoadItems"
                     Placeholder="Select items"
                     InitialSelectedItems="initialSelectedItems"
                     NameSelectors="nameSelectors" />
    </div>
</DemoExample>

